   EEnnccooddiinngg ooff IInntteeggeerrss
     Integers, which are of type CCTTFF__KK__IINNTTEEGGEERR, have no variable length argu‐
     ments.  Instead, they are followed by a uuiinntt3322__tt which describes their
     encoding.  All integers must be encoded with a variable length of zero.
     The _c_t_t___s_i_z_e member describes the length of the integer in bytes.  In
     general, integer sizes will be rounded up to the closest power of two.

     The integer encoding contains three different pieces of information:
           ••   The encoding of the integer
           ••   The offset in bbiittss of the type
           ••   The size in bbiittss of the type

     This encoding can be expressed through the following macros:

           #define CTF_INT_ENCODING(data)  (((data) & 0xff000000) >> 24)
           #define CTF_INT_OFFSET(data)    (((data) & 0x00ff0000) >> 16)
           #define CTF_INT_BITS(data)      (((data) & 0x0000ffff))

           #define CTF_INT_DATA(encoding, offset, bits) \
                   (((encoding) << 24) | ((offset) << 16) | (bits))

     The following flags are defined for the encoding at this time:

           #define CTF_INT_SIGNED          0x01
           #define CTF_INT_CHAR            0x02
           #define CTF_INT_BOOL            0x04
           #define CTF_INT_VARARGS         0x08

     By default, an integer is considered to be unsigned, unless it has the
     CCTTFF__IINNTT__SSIIGGNNEEDD flag set.  If the flag CCTTFF__IINNTT__CCHHAARR is set, that indicates
     that the integer is of a type that stores character data, for example the
     intrinsic C type cchhaarr would have the CCTTFF__IINNTT__CCHHAARR flag set.  If the flag
     CCTTFF__IINNTT__BBOOOOLL is set, that indicates that the integer represents a boolean
     type.  For example, the intrinsic C type __BBooooll would have the
     CCTTFF__IINNTT__BBOOOOLL flag set.  Finally, the flag CCTTFF__IINNTT__VVAARRAARRGGSS indicates that
     the integer is used as part of a variable number of arguments.  This en‐
     coding is rather uncommon.

